From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:06:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a theme cap a text's lines, ending the last with an
 ellipsis

A wrapped text could only grow or be cut by its box: a long title
pushed the lines under it down, or ran into them, and a description
stopped in the middle of a line at the box's edge. The text element's
maxLines keeps at most that many lines; the last one ends with an
ellipsis where the text goes on, and a text sized "w 0" is as tall as
the lines it keeps, so the elements stacked under it follow.
---
